===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|sparhauk}}, {{m|enm|sperhauk}}, from {{inh|en|ang|spearhafoc}}, {{m|ang|spearhabuc|t=sparrow-hawk}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sparwahabuk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sparwahabukaz}}, equivalent to {{com|en|sparrow|hawk}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|spurvehøg|t=sparrowhawk}}, {{cog|sv|sparvhök|t=sparrowhawk}}, {{cog|is|sparrhaukur|t=sparrowhawk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-sparrowhawk.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[Eurasian sparrowhawk]], {{taxfmt|Accipiter nisus|species}}, a small, short-winged [[European]] [[hawk]] that preys on smaller birds.
## {{lb|en|falconry}} A [[female]] such bird, a male being a [[musket]].
# Any of numerous other relatively small birds of [[Old World]] species of {{taxfmt|Accipiter|genus}}, that prey on smaller birds or otherwise resemble ''A. nisus''.
# {{alternative form of|en|sparrow hawk}}; [[American kestrel]], {{taxfmt|Falco sparverius|species}}, of similar size and habit.

